And after some time I just jumped in and we're talking with John about it last year.

914
01:03:45,510 --> 01:03:47,910
And I think what we found out is.

915
01:03:47,910 --> 01:03:49,910
that John by himself is not sure what he means by deep modules.

916
01:03:49,910 --> 01:03:56,309
because he's not sure whe they were talking about implementation there or not talking about implementation.

917
01:03:56,309 --> 01:04:00,630
And I had this gut feeling when I was starting the book that this need to be clarified.

918
01:04:00,630 --> 01:04:05,990
But I didn't know what exactly would come from it.

919
01:04:05,990 --> 01:04:11,349
and actually redefining it and saying okay let's let's talk about deep interfaces.

920
01:04:11,349 --> 01:04:13,190
and leave everything else to saying like.

921
01:04:13,190 --> 01:04:16,789
okay we don't want modules to be dysfunctional that's a separate topic.

922
01:04:16,789 --> 01:04:21,750
let's just decouple it a little bit and just focus on interfaces when we're talking about depth.

923
01:04:21,750 --> 01:04:24,069
that was uh pretty big revelation.

924
01:04:24,079 --> 01:04:30,150
so when you say a deep interface versus a shallow interface what exactly are you describing?

925
01:04:30,160 --> 01:04:32,390
Yeah.

926
01:04:32,390 --> 01:04:35,109
So that's basically again value for money.

927
01:04:35,109 --> 01:04:40,230
How much functionality does the interface promise in turn for the complexity of the interface.

928
01:04:40,230 --> 01:04:44,870
So you can think of it as like uh functionality divided by complexity of the interface.

929
01:04:44,880 --> 01:04:50,470
So a narrow interface that does a lot for you versus a broad interface. that does very little for you.

930
01:04:50,480 --> 01:04:53,671
Exactly. Yeah. Okay. Great.

